================================================================================
SCOPE, AND TWO CARVE-OUTS
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers this project's OWN work: everything under `toolkit/`
and `schema/overrides.json`, the documentation, and the research in `studies/`.

1. CONTENT ROWS SOURCED FROM THE GUILD WARS WIKI.

   `content/*.toml` carries per-row provenance, and 26 rows record
   `source = "wiki"` (22 in `content/world.toml`, 4 in `content/maps.toml`).
   Those rows are derived from the Guild Wars Wiki (wiki.guildwars.com), which
   is dual-licensed GFDL 1.2 / CC BY-NC-SA 2.5. They carry the wiki's terms,
   not MIT — attribution is required, and the ShareAlike and NonCommercial arms
   apply to them. Every such row names its page and revision id, so the set is
   identifiable rather than diffuse. The rest of `content/` is MIT like the
   code.

2. THIRD-PARTY WORK THIS PROJECT BUILDS ON.

   Several modules take an algorithm, a file layout or a constant table from an
   upstream project. Each is registered in PLAN.md section 6.1 and credited in
   THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, which reproduces the licence text where the licence
   asks for it. Those terms travel with the code that uses them.

================================================================================
WHAT IS NOT LICENSED HERE, BECAUSE IT IS NOT OURS TO LICENSE
================================================================================

Guild Wars, `Gw.exe` and `Gw.dat` are ArenaNet's. This repository contains none
of their bytes and never has: no client files, no extracted assets, no
decompiled code. See the header of `.gitignore` for the rationale and CLAUDE.md
for the boundary this project holds itself to. Nothing above grants any right
in ArenaNet's software or content, and running this server requires a copy of
the game that you bought yourself.
